## Tables related to Solution

Each of these hangs off `nx_solution` with a required N:1 lookup, and inherits the parent's visibility rules.

### `nx_demoasset` — the demo

The curated, presentable asset a CSM opens and shows. Unchanged from v1.

| Column | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Name *(primary name)* | Text (100) | Yes | |
| Solution | Lookup → `nx_solution` | Yes | |
| Asset Type | Choice — global | Yes | Self-contained HTML · Hosted web app (URL) · Power Apps · Power BI · Desktop app or script · Video walkthrough · One-pager / slide |
| File | File | No | For self-contained HTML |
| External URL | URL (500) | No | For hosted/embedded links |
| Allows Embedding | Yes/No | No | |
| Sort Order | Whole Number | No | |

### `nx_demorequest` — the live-demo ask

The "request a live demo" escape hatch, and a signal of which solutions the business actually pulls on.

| Column | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Name *(primary name)* | Text (100) | Yes | Auto: "{Solution name} — {Requester}" |
| Solution | Lookup → `nx_solution` | Yes | |
| Requested By | Lookup → `systemuser` | Yes | |
| Client / Opportunity Context | Text, multi-line (1000) | No | |
| Needed By | Date Only | No | |
| Request Status | Choice — global | Yes | New · Acknowledged · Scheduled · Delivered · Declined |

### `nx_project` — the evidence

Proof that a solution has actually been delivered somewhere. Does **not** carry the demo — that stays on `nx_demoasset` above.

| Column | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Project Name *(primary name)* | Text (100) | Yes | |
| Solution | Lookup → `nx_solution` | **No** | A project can be logged before anyone knows which Solution it belongs to. An empty value is the Librarian's queue of work still to classify. |
| Client / Industry | Text (200) | Yes | Internal-only |
| What Was Delivered | Text, multi-line (2000) | Yes | The proof — what actually got built |
| Business Problem | Text, multi-line (1000) | No | Why the client needed it — carries the "what need does this solve" framing now that there's no separate category tag |
| Project Owner | Lookup → `systemuser` | Yes | |
| Source | Choice — global | No | Manual Entry · GitHub |
| External Link | URL (500) | No | GitHub repo, Power BI workspace, or Power Apps link |
| Documentation | URL (500) | No | |
| Date Delivered | Date Only | No | |

Tags into `nx_technology` (N:N) — the specific stack used on this delivery.

